  ],
  "secondary_categories": [],
  "slug": "simulations-structural-6310",
  "summary": "BioEmu2 emulates biomolecular dynamics far faster than MD, while enhanced-sampling studies resolve multimodal binding landscapes in disordered regions.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is the shift from single static structures toward conformational ensembles and dynamics. BioEmu2 generates atomically resolved structures and dynamics at sampling rates far above molecular dynamics. The FCP1 study applies OneOPES enhanced-sampling MD to a disordered region binding Rap74, revealing a multimodal conformational landscape and introducing a Divide et impera free-energy decomposition. ProtFlap approaches flexibility from the static side, predicting residue-level flexibility from single structures with an atomic energy-based graph neural network trained on RMSF labels. The AlphaFold analysis of experimentally validated non-globular proteins shows where static predictions diverge from biologically relevant states, which bears on the limits of single-structure models. GlycoMarinate extends the toolkit to coarse-grained Martini 3 modelling of N-glycoproteins. What is new is the use of generative emulation and explicit free-energy decomposition of multimodal binding, although the items do not establish a shared benchmark across these methods.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
